<div class="box wide">
  <div class="story_text">
    <p>
      Thneed is a public discussion site. Stories, comments, votes where shown,
      profiles, invitation relationships, and moderation records are public and
      may be copied or archived by others.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we keep</h2>

    <p>
      Accounts require an email address for login, invitations, password
      recovery, and operational messages. We do not display account email
      addresses publicly. Thneed uses a session cookie to keep members signed
      in and preference cookies where needed for site operation.
    </p>

    <p>
      Like most web services, our server and security systems process
      operational logs that may include IP addresses, request times, browser
      information, requested URLs, and errors. We use this data to operate,
      secure, debug, and prevent abuse of the site, and retain it only as long
      as operationally necessary.
    </p>

    <h2>Links and avatars</h2>

    <p>
      Submitted links lead to independently operated sites with their own
      privacy practices. To reduce routine disclosure to avatar providers,
      Thneed fetches configured external avatars and serves cached copies from
      its own domain.
    </p>

    <h2>Access and deletion</h2>

    <p>
      Moderators and operators may access account and operational information
      when needed for support, safety, abuse prevention, or legal compliance.
      They do not receive broader access merely to participate in discussion.
    </p>

    <p>
      Members can deactivate their account in settings. For an account deletion
      request or a privacy question, contact
      <a href="mailto:privacy@thneed.org">privacy@thneed.org</a>. We will remove
      or anonymize account data where practical, but public contributions may
      remain so existing discussions are not broken and copies held by others
      are outside our control.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
